# Top-level pins for the Python 3.8 row of python.yml, and nowhere else. This
# file exists only for that row and goes away with it; every other job installs
# ../python-bindings.txt (Python 3.10 and newer, fixed pytest).
#
# It lives in its own directory so that .github/dependabot.yml can hold pytest
# and typing-extensions back for this file alone: ignore rules apply per
# dependency name across a whole directory.
#
# pip-compile drops a requirement whose environment marker is false on the
# machine that compiles. So every dependency that holds only on some Python or
# OS is listed here unconditionally, with an exact pin: a pure-Python wheel that
# is harmless where the marker is false. Any compile of this file, on any
# Python (Dependabot compiles on its own), then resolves the same package set,
# and scripts/check_release_workflow.py fails a .txt whose set differs.
#   colorama           pytest, Windows only
#   exceptiongroup     pytest, Python < 3.11
#   tomli              pytest and maturin, Python < 3.11
#   typing-extensions  exceptiongroup, Python < 3.13
# Compile it on Python 3.8. pytest 8.4 needs Python 3.9+, so pytest is pinned
# to 8.3.5, and typing-extensions to the last release that supports 3.8
# (4.13.2).
#
# Refresh recipe: docs/CI.md, "Hashed Python requirements".
maturin==1.15.0
pytest==8.3.5
colorama==0.4.6
exceptiongroup==1.3.1
tomli==2.5.0
typing-extensions==4.13.2
